# One-shot removal of the dedukun/bookmarks.yazi plugin and the two yazi config
# files that existed only to configure it.
#
# Deleting a source entry makes chezmoi stop managing the target, but it does
# not delete the copy already in ~. This does.
#
# Delete this file once it has been applied everywhere. It takes effect on
# every apply, so leaving it in place would silently delete these paths again
# if they were ever recreated on purpose.
.config/yazi/plugins/bookmarks.yazi
.config/yazi/plugins
.config/yazi/init.lua
.config/yazi/keymap.toml
